1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,815
Why does a cold can sweat?

2
00:00:02,115 --> 00:00:03,922
The water isn't leaking out.

3
00:00:03,922 --> 00:00:05,083
The can is sealed.

4
00:00:05,583 --> 00:00:08,582
Warm air is full of invisible water vapour.

5
00:00:08,882 --> 00:00:15,006
On a hot, humid day, one cubic metre of air carries about 25 grams of it.

6
00:00:15,506 --> 00:00:20,223
The air touching a can from the fridge chills to nearly fridge temperature.

7
00:00:20,523 --> 00:00:25,820
That cold, no more than about six grams per cubic metre can stay as vapour.

8
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:31,647
The rest has nowhere to go, so it turns back into liquid, right on the can.

9
00:00:32,147 --> 00:00:38,650
It's the same as morning dew, or the fog on your glasses when you step out of an air-conditioned room.

10
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:40,720
The can isn't sweating.

11
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:41,471
The air is.
